  "solution": {
    "text": "The rate of hydrolysis will depend on how likely a molecule is to accepting &nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; ions. Rate of hydrolysis&nbsp;<math><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp; effect or <math><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi></math> of ester.&nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi></math>. <math><mo>-</mo><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp; is a strong <math><mi>E</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>G</mi></math> (Electron withdrawing group),<math><mo>-</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></math> is a weak <math><mi>E</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>G</mi></math> and <math><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is an <math><mi>E</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi></math>(Electron donating group).",
